---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import WhatsAppLink from '../components/WhatsAppLink.astro';
import { solarSources } from '../data/solar';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Residential Solar & PM Surya Ghar Guide | Incetekh Energy"
  description="Plan a rooftop solar installation in Andhra Pradesh: household subsidy, roof requirements, power-cut backup, panel care and practical answers."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Make an informed choice"
    title="Solar, clearly explained."
    description="From your first electricity bill to caring for an installed system. Practical guidance for your home or business."
  />
  <div class="container guide">
    <nav aria-label="In this guide">
      <a class="text-link" href="#residential">
        Residential solar
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="#subsidy">
        Subsidy
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="#maintenance">
        Maintenance
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="#faq">
        Questions
      </a>
    </nav>
    <section id="residential" class="prose">
      <h2>Start with your home.</h2>
      <p>
        Bring your last 12 months of electricity use, your site location and a
        roof photograph if available. A site visit checks usable space, shade,
        roof condition, access and the electrical connection before choosing
        capacity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Panels generate electricity; an inverter converts it for use in the
        building. A grid-connected system works alongside your electricity
        supply. Batteries and backup-capable equipment are a separate design
        choice.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Estimate your size from your average monthly bill.</li>
        <li>Arrange a free site visit and review the proposed layout.</li>
        <li>
          Confirm equipment, approvals, written pricing and warranty terms
          before ordering.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keep commissioning records, warranties and a baseline generation
          report for future checks.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link" href="/#solar-planner">
        Find your solar size
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/#site-visit">
        Arrange a free site visit
      </a>
    </section>
    <section id="subsidy" class="prose">
      <h2>PM Surya Ghar: household support.</h2>
      <p>
        The programme remains active in official government updates checked on
        30 September 2026. For a new eligible household rooftop installation in
        Andhra Pradesh, standard central assistance is:
      </p>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>1 kW</dt>
          <dd>Up to ₹30,000</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>2 kW</dt>
          <dd>Up to ₹60,000</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>3 kW or more</dt>
          <dd>Up to ₹78,000</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p>
        Rates are ₹30,000 per kW for the first 2 kW and ₹18,000 for the next kW.
        The cap does not increase for larger individual household systems.
        Commercial connections and solar water heaters do not qualify for this
        household PV subsidy; state top-ups are not included here.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Register on the National Portal with your electricity connection
          details.
        </li>
        <li>
          Follow your DISCOM's current application and approval process before
          installation.
        </li>
        <li>
          Choose a registered vendor and equipment meeting the scheme's
          domestic-content requirements.
        </li>
        <li>
          Complete inspection, commissioning and the portal's bank/subsidy
          steps.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Approval and payment are conditional, not an automatic discount.
        Existing installations, extensions and previously claimed assistance
        need an individual eligibility check.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={solarSources.portal}>
        Open the official application portal
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={solarSources.subsidy}>
        Check central rates
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={solarSources.status}>
        Read the government update
      </a>
    </section>
    <section id="maintenance" class="prose">
      <h2>Keep your system performing.</h2>
      <p>
        Compare generation over similar weather periods and watch for inverter
        alerts. A sudden sustained drop, new shading or visible damage is a
        reason to request a check.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Follow the module maker's cleaning instructions. Avoid abrasive
          chemicals and pressure washing.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use trained help for roof access, cleaning near wiring and electrical
          inspections. Do not walk on panels or open electrical equipment.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keep drainage and access paths clear. Check for new tree growth or
          construction that creates shade.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keep generation records and your equipment warranty documents
          together.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Incetekh offers free system performance checks and free annual yield
        audits. Contact us to discuss your installation and arrange a visit.
      </p>
      <WhatsAppLink
        label="Request a performance check"
        message="Hi Incetekh, I would like to arrange a free system performance check."
      />
    </section>
    <section id="faq" class="prose">
      <h2>Before you decide.</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>Can solar run two ACs and fans?</summary>
        <p>
          It can offset the energy they use, but appliance counts alone do not
          size a system. Wattage, hours of use, other loads and available
          sunlight matter. Our 3 kW family-home illustration allows limited
          daytime AC use; it does not promise continuous operation or power-cut
          backup.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does on-grid solar work during a power cut?</summary>
        <p>
          A standard grid-tied inverter shuts down when the grid fails. Backup
          requires a compatible system designed for islanded operation, often
          with a battery. Ask for the supported backup loads in writing.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How much roof space is needed?</summary>
        <p>
          For early planning, allow about 10 m² (108 sq ft) of clear roof per
          kW. Access, shading, tilt and the final layout can change that
          allowance. A 3 kW example needs about 30 m² (323 sq ft).
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={solarSources.faq}>
          Utility rooftop guidance
        </a>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will my electricity bill become zero?</summary>
        <p>
          Not necessarily. Fixed and demand charges, consumption outside solar
          hours, export settlement and your actual tariff affect the bill. Our
          calculator uses disclosed assumptions rather than promising a zero
          bill.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens to extra generation?</summary>
        <p>
          Grid export requires the approved metering arrangement. Your DISCOM's
          rules determine how exports are credited or settled. Confirm these
          terms and the permitted system capacity before ordering.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I finance the installation?</summary>
        <p>
          Some banks offer residential rooftop solar loans, subject to their
          lending rules. Compare the loan's total cost with the written
          installation quote and your expected savings.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/financing/">
          Explore solar financing
        </a>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which products and warranties apply?</summary>
        <p>
          Panel, inverter and water-heater options are listed in our catalogue.
          Stock, suitability and manufacturer warranties depend on the selected
          model. Incetekh's 5-year warranty is subject to the written proposal
          and applicable terms.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/products/">
          Products we install
        </a>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
  .guide {
    max-width: 64rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }
  nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding-block: 3rem;
    scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  li {
    margin-block: 0.75rem;
  }
  ul,
  ol {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .text-link {
    margin-right: 1.5rem;
  }
  dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #e8ede3;
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  details p {
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 36rem) {
    dl {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
